# Go sources and documents are stored and checked out with LF on every platform,
# so a Windows checkout does not read as a modification of every file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts used by the laboratory and the release process keep LF as well.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Sealed evidence is hashed over the bytes on disk. Git must never convert these
# files on checkout: a CRLF rewrite would break every signature in the bundle,
# and a byte added to a delivered document fails the same check.
runs/** -text
publications/** -text
